# Force LF for anything that runs inside Linux containers or on a Linux server,
# regardless of core.autocrlf on a given contributor's/deploy machine's Windows
# checkout. Without this, `git archive`/checkout on Windows can silently turn
# LF into CRLF for these files, which breaks shebang lines (`/usr/bin/env bash\r`
# => "No such file or directory") when deployed to a Linux host.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
Caddyfile*      text eol=lf
*.rs            text eol=lf
